Third-Party Software, Fonts, and Specifications Notice
===============================================================================

This project incorporates code, architectural designs, fonts, and specifications
from the following open-source projects and standards:

1. omml-converter (Rust)
   Original Project: https://github.com/bohdanbodnarenko/omml-converter
   Author: Bohdan Bodnarenko
   License: MIT License
   Copyright (c) 2024-2026 Bohdan Bodnarenko
   Description:
     Initial architecture for forward (OMML → MathType OLE) conversion, .docx
     package manipulation, and MTEF 5.0 binary generation.

2. mathtypejx (Java)
   Original Project: https://github.com/a917470154/mathtypejx
   Author: a917470154
   License: MIT License
   Description:
     Ported and referenced for reverse conversion: MTEF v3 and v5 binary stream
     decoding, MathML node tree construction, template selector/variation bitmasks,
     sub/superscript base-mover logic, and MathType character mapping tables.

3. mathtype_to_mathml (Ruby)
   Original Project: https://github.com/jure/mathtype_to_mathml
   Author: Jure Triglav
   License: MIT License
   Description:
     Reference implementation and binary test fixtures for MTEF reverse engineering.

4. STIX Fonts Project (STIX Two Text & STIX Two Math)
   Official Project: https://github.com/stipub/stixfonts
   Copyright (c) 2001-2021, The STI Pub Companies
   License: SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1
   License Location: assets/fonts/stixfonts-2.13b171/OFL.txt
   Description:
     Embedded OpenType fonts in `assets/fonts/` used for vector (EMF) and raster (PNG)
     equation preview rendering, glyph outline extraction, and OpenType 'MATH' table
     metric constants.

5. Technical Specifications and Standards:
   - ECMA-376 (Office Open XML File Formats, §22.1 Office Math Markup Language - OMML)
     ISO/IEC 29500
   - Microsoft OpenType Specification: The 'MATH' Table
     https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/typography/opentype/spec/math
   - Design Science MathType MTEF v3 and v5 Binary Format Specifications
     http://www.dessci.com/en/support/mathtype/tech/mtef5.htm
   - Donald E. Knuth, The TeXbook, Appendix G: "Generating Boxes from Formulas"
     Addison-Wesley, 1984
   - W3C MathML Core Specification
     https://w3c.github.io/mathml-core/

Native desktop UI
-----------------
The native desktop uses egui/eframe (MIT OR Apache-2.0), rfd (MIT),
arboard (MIT OR Apache-2.0), interprocess (0BSD OR Apache-2.0), fs2
(MIT OR Apache-2.0), directories (MIT OR Apache-2.0), ureq
(MIT OR Apache-2.0), image (MIT OR Apache-2.0), and tempfile
(MIT OR Apache-2.0), together with their platform dependencies.
Cargo.lock records resolved versions; cargo-deny checks the workspace license
policy. Bundled STIX fonts retain the SIL Open Font License attribution above.
